- How would you test tenant isolation and data leakage risks?
- Describe a canary deployment strategy for new model versions in SageMaker.
- What monitoring dashboards and SLOs would you implement for latency and accuracy?
- How would you handle model drift and feature changes across tenants?

## Why This Is Asked

Tests end-to-end real-time pipeline design, AI inference integration, privacy controls, and cost trade-offs in production-scale systems.

## Key Concepts

- Event-driven architecture and streaming integration (WebSocket, Kinesis, Lambda)
- SageMaker endpoint invocation and model monitoring
- PII redaction strategies and compliance (encryption, access controls, retention)
- Data lake indexing (S3, DynamoDB) and cost implications

## Code Example

```javascript
import { SageMakerRuntimeClient, InvokeEndpointCommand } from "@aws-sdk/client-sagemaker-runtime";

const client = new SageMakerRuntimeClient({ region: 'us-east-1' });

async function analyze(message){
  const cmd = new InvokeEndpointCommand({
    EndpointName: 'chat-sentiment-intent',
    ContentType: 'text/plain',
    Body: message
  });
  const res = await client.send(cmd);
  return JSON.parse(res.Body.toString());
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you test privacy controls and retention policies end-to-end?
- How would you handle backpressure and scale Lambda consumptions?
- What monitoring would you add for model drift and data leakage risk?

Why This Is Asked

Tests the ability to design a scalable, privacy-aware, vendor-integrated NLP pipeline that processes structured chat data in JSONL format, with PII redaction, cross-account sharing, and cost-aware inference choices.

## Key Concepts

- Event-driven architectures (S3 events, Step Functions)
- Lambda for lightweight processing and redaction
- Amazon Comprehend for NER/Sentiment
- SageMaker for topic modeling and batch inference
- Data governance: IAM, KMS, encryption, access control
- Observability: CloudWatch, X-Ray, metrics, traces
- Cross-account sharing patterns and vendor approvals

## Code Example

```javascript
// Lambda: simple PII redaction sketch
exports.handler = async (event) => {
  const body = JSON.parse(event.body);
  body.messages = body.messages.map(m => m.replace(/[A-Z0-9._%+-]+@[A-Z0-9.-]+\.[A-Z]{2,4}/gi, '[REDACTED_EMAIL]'));
  return { statusCode: 200, body: JSON.stringify(body) };
};
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you measure latency and cold-start impact for this pipeline at scale?
- How would you implement data retention policies and automated revocation of access for vendors?
